Five verdict strings can come back; the first two are outcomes, the rest are reasons the test refused to answer at all:
Verdict string
Meaning
A_BETTER / B_BETTER
The test ran and found a statistically significant loss difference at the configured alpha
NO_SIGNIFICANT_DIFF
The test ran; the p-value cleared alpha, or the two forecasters' errors were numerically indistinguishable
INSUFFICIENT_SAMPLE
Fewer bars than the manifest's min_sample_size were available - no test was attempted
INVALID_HORIZON
horizon was zero or negative, or (less obviously) large enough relative to n that the HLN correction term itself goes negative under the radical - both are rejected explicitly rather than letting MathSqrt() return NaN
INVALID_VARIANCE
The HAC variance estimate came back negative - a numerically invalid result, not a "no difference" one
The loss differential is computed bar by bar as d_t = L(e1_t) - L(e2_t), using whichever loss function was chosen:
