The test statistic is built from the sample mean of d_t divided by an estimate of its standard error: DM = d_bar / sqrt(V_hat / T), where V_hat is the long-run variance of d_bar. Rather than the naive sample variance of d_t, the HAC estimator sums the autocovariances at every lag up to h-1 (h being the forecast horizon), weighted down with a Bartlett kernel so distant lags contribute less. The autocovariance at a given lag is a small helper function on its own:
DM_Autocovariance
